#? **** HTK: HMM ToolKit
{<author> Fu Jie Huang}

This is an interface to Cambridge University's Hidden Markov Model ToolKit.
Updated for {<b> HTK version 3.4.1}, which adds discriminative training
(MMI/MPE/MWE), lattice-based forward-backward, MAP estimation, and
a rewritten speaker adaptation framework (XForms).

HTK source is available from {<hlink> https://github.com/open-speech/HTK}.

#? *** Installation

The Lush interface needs {<c> libhtk.a} (static library) and header files
installed under {<c> ~/.lush/local/}. To build from source:
{<code>
1. Download: wget -O HTK.tar.gz https://github.com/open-speech/HTK/archive/master.tar.gz
2. Extract: tar xzf HTK.tar.gz && cd HTK-master
3. Patch for 64-bit: sed -i 's/-m32 -ansi/-fPIC -ansi/g' configure
4. Configure: ./configure --prefix=~/.lush/local --disable-hslab --without-x
5. Build: cd HTKLib && make
6. Install library: cp HTKLiblv.a ~/.lush/local/lib/libhtk.a
7. Install headers: cp *.h ~/.lush/local/include/htk/
</code>}

Start Lush and type:
{<code>
	? (libload "htk/htk")
</code>}

